<title>AUSTRALIA: By Ian Pemberton.</title>
<headline>By Ian Pemberton.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>FAI Insurances Ltd chief executive Rodney Adler said on Thursday that he was concerned about the possible impact of the abandoned sale of its New Zealand and Pacific islands general insurance unit on staff and the company's reputation in the region.</p>
<p>Adler said Australian Stock Exchange disclosure rules meant the sale talks had to be revealed when the sale was not guaranteed. He said FAI had no intention of selling the profitable unit until it was approached with a top-price A$50 million offer from rival insurer MMI Ltd.</p>
</text>
